    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0337" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg267"/>

                <head>No. 130.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Morton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-04-26"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 26,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 267.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 333, of the 13th instant,
                    inclosing a copy of a petition addressed to the minister of commerce by French
                    importers and dealers in American pork, has been read with interest as a
                    valuable indication of the tendency of sound opinion in France on the
                    question.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
